      "time": "in-text",
      "time_notes": "Each turn-pair item carries 'Time anchor: <event_time>' in its text, as cognee's BEAM preprocessing does. temporal_cognify stays off, as in cognee's BEAM ingestion. cognee.search takes no query date, so query_time is ignored and applied_settings says so. A null event_time (allowed by the protocol) is written as 'Time anchor: unknown'; cognee never substitutes the ingest time, because dates live only in the text.",
      "provenance": {
        "status": "partial",
        "mechanism": "Chunk items carry payload.document_id, which is the cognee Data id. The shim pins each session's Data id (uuid5 of namespace and source id) through DataItem.data_id and labels it with the source id, so a chunk maps to exactly one session (exact). Entity and fact items come from the merged graph and carry no source; they are returned with provenance unavailable. The map is rebuilt from cognee.datasets.list_data labels (public API) after a restart."
      },
      "delete": "native",
      "delete_notes": "cognee.forget(data_id, dataset) removes the Data row and its chunks and chunk vectors; after it no chunk from the deleted session returns. In the keyless check (canned extraction), graph entities shared with a surviving session stayed and their edge text still quoted the deleted session; in the metered smoke (real extraction) no entity or fact mentioned the deleted fact. lifecycle-lite should score entity and fact items as well as chunks.",
      "readiness": "synchronous: /ingest runs cognee.add then cognee.cognify(run_in_background=False) for that session, as cognee's BEAM local_ingest does, so /finish has nothing to wait for. A failed pipeline raises (raise_on_error=True) and becomes a product_error.",
      "namespace": "dataset (one cognee dataset per namespace, named by the opaque ns id; ENABLE_BACKEND_ACCESS_CONTROL is on by default, so each dataset gets its own graph and vector store)",
      "parallel_namespaces": false,
      "retrieval_policies": {
        "vendor-default": {
          "top_k": 15,
          "maps_to": "cognee.search(query_type=HYBRID_COMPLETION, only_context=True, verbose=True, datasets=[ns]). search top_k 15 caps each hybrid lane at min(15, DEFAULT_HYBRID_LANE_TOP_K=10): 10 chunks, 10 entities with up to 10 edges each, 10 facts. HYBRID_COMPLETION is recall()'s fallback type (ROUTER_FALLBACK_TYPE) and the retriever cognee selected for its reported BEAM configuration. The type is pinned (auto_route off) so the item shape is deterministic."
        },
        "fixed-evidence": {
          "top_k": 15,
          "chunks_top_k": 20,
          "entities_top_k": 20,
          "maps_to": "cognee.search(query_type=HYBRID_COMPLETION, only_context=True, verbose=True, datasets=[ns]). 20 chunks, 20 entities (cognee's reported BEAM 100K configuration hybrid_completion_20_20_qa_v1), 10 facts; the harness packs the returned items to the 8,000-token budget. Why: the largest documented hybrid setting; the harness truncates to the shared budget"
        }
      },
